  "conclusions": [
    "No one of the four primary pathway scores demonstrated association with clinical benefit: all BH-adjusted q values are0.5210. This is not evidence of equivalence or absence of a biological role.",
    "The primary rank-score medians are lower in the clinical-benefit group for all four programs. The shifts are uncertain and do not support selecting high bulk TGF-beta/CAF/ECM expression as a positive vactosertib biomarker.",
    "The two objective responders have lower LRRC15-CAF and c-ECM point estimates, but neither is significant (separate-family q0.4444). With two responses, this is descriptive and cannot establish a low-stroma response rule.",
    "Prespecified stricter-universe, log-TPM, dose-stratified and joint dose/liver-stratified sensitivities do not produce a nominal P<0.05. Hallmark and c-ECM clinical-benefit median directions change under log scoring, underscoring metric dependence.",
    "This single-arm selected paired-RNA subset cannot separate treatment prediction from prognosis, tissue composition or other confounding, and cannot attribute associations specifically to vactosertib rather than pembrolizumab or their combination.",
    "These results add no validated efficacy upgrade for vactosertib based on the case's archival stromal profile or SMAD4 variant. They also do not exclude benefit or invalidate stromal biology; current-node mechanism and individual response probability remain unestablished."
  ],
  "material_limits": [
    "Only5 clinical-benefit cases and2 objective responders; effect confidence intervals are not implemented in the frozen analysis. Do not interpret nonsignificance as equivalence.",
    "The28-subject paired-RNA subset is not the full trial efficacy population;2/28 is not a replacement for the published full-trial response rate.",
    "23/28 screening-to-post-treatment specimen collection intervals exceed90days (median834days). This is not the interval from specimen collection to first dose; unknown biopsy organ and purity limit interpretation.",
    "Both objective responders received200mg twice daily and lacked liver in the supplied baseline site lists. Clinical benefit is also imbalanced by dose/liver. TMB varies in both groups, with one benefit value missing and the nonbenefit range reaching74.02.",
    "The secondary joint dose/liver test has only21 admissible allocations in one7-person informative stratum. Its two-sided distinct-score minimum is2/21, so it is intrinsically coarse.",
    "Mapping varies4.70-39.23% of retained pairs, with11/28 below20%; coding-depth and directional-library heterogeneity remain limits despite full technical admission and broad gene coverage.",
    "Unweighted mean-rank scores use fixed published memberships, not every original publication's weighting/scoring model; no validated clinical cutoffs are transferred.",
    "No untreated/comparator arm, treatment interaction, current-case RNA calibration, SMAD4 subgroup test, paired on-treatment efficacy test, or external validation is supplied."
  ],
  "nonblocking_reporting_corrections": [
    "Use clinical benefit with its explicit definition; historical frozen source labels that say durable clinical benefit must not imply every response lasted6months.",
    "The assembled QC table library_types column is blank because Salmon2.8 uses detected_library_type. Use independently admitted library_type values (24ISR/4IU); this ancillary field is not used in scoring.",
    "Preserve source and audit boundaries: raw FASTQs were MD5-verified before task-only cleanup; final admission independently rehashed retained native outputs and checked raw/cleaned receipts, but cannot rehash deleted FASTQs again."
  ],
  "recommended_report_sentence": "In all28 available baseline trial RNA samples, none of four prespecified TGF-beta, fibroblast or extracellular-matrix programs was significantly associated with study-defined clinical benefit after four-test correction (allq=0.521). This small, archival, single-arm analysis does not validate high pathway expression as a vactosertib-selection biomarker and does not rule out benefit.",
